<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amage</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amage was a Sarmatian queen known from the Stratagems of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polyaenus">Polyaenus</a>. Taking power from her husband, who was given to drink, she ruled and commanded the army herself. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scythians">Scythians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crimea">Crimea</a> threatened the Greek city of Chersonesus, she rode with a small picked force against the Scythian royal seat, killed the king and installed his son as an ally. She is often cited as evidence of women's power among the Sarmatians.</p></div>
